model_output_raw:
The following code creates a simple login page using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It includes placeholders for the username and password fields, a submit button, and a login message. It uses a simple form submit event handler to capture credentials. The login page will only prompt the user to enter their credentials and display a message if they are correct.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Login Page</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; padding: 20px; text-align: center; }
        h1 { color: #333; }
        .form-group { margin-bottom: 10px; }
        input[type="text"], input[type="password"] { width: 100%; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        button { padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; background-color: #4CAF50; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
        #login-message { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 1rem; color: green; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Login</h1>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label for="username">Username:</label>
        <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Enter your username here" required>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label for="password">Password:</label>
        <input type="password" id="password" placeholder="Enter your password here" required>
    </div>

    <button onclick="loginUser()">Login</button>

    <div id="login-message"></div>

    <script>
        function loginUser() {
            const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
            const password = document.getElementById('password').value;
            const message = document.getElementById('login-message');

            if (username.trim().length === 0 || password.trim().length === 0) {
                message.textContent = 'Please enter both username and password.';
                return;
            }

            message.textContent = 'Login successful! You are now logged in.';
            document.getElementById('username').value = '';
            document.getElementById('password').value = '';
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

This script creates a simple login form that captures the user's input. The login message will appear after the user enters their credentials. The form is styled with basic CSS.

